+CI reads this table and builds each distinct `(arch, defconfig, dtb, image)`
+tuple once in the matching ARM32 or ARM64 lane. The ARM64 lane runs
+`olddefconfig`, builds `Image dtbs` with the AArch64 GCC/linker flags, and
+asserts `CONFIG_COMPAT=y`. The ARM32 lane keeps the ARMHF GCC/linker flags and
+its resolved-configuration checks.
+
+A publication matrix covers all targets and uploads
+`libreecho-kernel-<target>-<image>`, `-dtb`, `-System.map` and `-config`. Existing
+ARM32 targets still publish `libreecho-kernel-<target>-zImage`, and Lidar
+publishes `libreecho-kernel-lidar-Image`. At parity the ARM32 images are copies
+of the same build outputs. The legacy Radar bundle
+`libreecho-linux-arm32-<sha>` is also retained. Changing a target tuple to valid
+in-tree sources adds a build lane automatically; unknown IDs, malformed fields
+or missing sources fail validation.
 
